{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For your seed shall be a sojourner</b> This verse is inverted (מְסֹרָס), and its proper ordering is: 'For your seed shall be sojourners in a land that is not theirs, four hundred years, and they shall serve them and they shall afflict them' — and Scripture did not specify how many days the servitude and affliction would last. And there are many inverted verses in Scripture. Thus: 'The Hebrew servant came to me, whom you brought to us, to mock me' (Genesis 39:17), and thus: 'And all the earth came to Egypt to buy grain from Joseph' (Genesis 41:57), and thus: 'For whoever eats leavened bread, that soul shall be cut off from Israel, from the first day until the seventh day' (Exodus 12:15), and thus: 'On that day a man shall cast away his idols of silver and his idols of gold, which they made for him, to worship to the porches and to the bats' (Isaiah 2:20), and thus: 'Come, hear, and I will declare to all who fear Elohim what He has done for my soul' (Psalms 66:16), and thus: 'To Me they cry: My Elohim, we know You, Israel' (Hosea 8:2), and thus: 'They shall be Mine, says YHWH of hosts, on the day that I make a treasured possession, and I will spare them' (Malachi 3:17), and many like these. And the meaning of the verse is: even though I say to you, 'To your seed I have given this land,' know well that before I give it to them, they shall be sojourners in a land that is not theirs for four hundred years, and moreover they shall serve them and they shall afflict them. And Rabbi Abraham said: 'Know well that your seed shall be sojourners' — in servitude and affliction — until the end of four hundred years from this day, and if so, He informed him of the end of the redemption but did not inform him how long the days of exile would be. This too is correct."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:47.269481562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}